# CTOgo: clean, low-friction copy

People skim. They do not want to read unless they choose to.

## Do
- Prefer one short sentence over paragraphs on primary UI (forms, checkboxes, CTAs, tooltips).
- Put detail behind optional links: “How it works”, Fees, FAQ.
- Keep product surfaces focused: what to do next, what it costs, what happens.
- Move protocol edge cases (abandonment, inactivity sweeps, treasury routing, rent math) to FAQ / Fees — not into the main flow.

## Don’t
- Write like an internal eng/product note (“rent/tx from the $1, remainder to treasury”, “platform fee still applies if you skip”).
- Stack long explainer boxes, rule dumps, or multi-step policy text on List / Launch / claim screens.
- Overwhelm first-time users with every protocol rule at once.

## Pattern
1. **Inline** — shortest helpful line.
2. **How it works** — only the mental model (fees → vault fill → spends unlock).
3. **FAQ / Fees** — abandonment, inactivity, fee math, edge cases.
